::JOUR_U05_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.02] Source: Storyboard: Hallway Recycling Video. Project Goal: Create a 30-second news video showing how students should use the new hallway recycling stations. Sequence: Shot 1 wide shot of the hallway station. Shot 2 close-up of the labels for paper, bottles, and trash. Shot 3 student holds a plastic bottle and pauses before choosing a bin. Shot 4 student places the bottle in the correct bin. Shot 5 final screen says Check the label before you drop it. Sound Plan: Short narration explains each step. Light background sound is allowed only if it does not cover the narration. Accuracy Note: The video must show the real labels and correct bin placement so viewers do not learn the wrong process. Question 1: Why should the storyboard begin with a wide shot? {
